          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>Under $H_0$, $\\bar x \\sim N(100,\\ \\sigma/\\sqrt n = 2/4 = 0.5)$. The boundaries standardise to $z=\\dfrac{98.5-100}{0.5}=-3$ and $z=\\dfrac{101.5-100}{0.5}=3$. So $\\alpha = P(\\bar x < 98.5) + P(\\bar x > 101.5) = 0.00135 + (1-0.99865) = 0.0027$.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>Dưới $H_0$, $\\bar x \\sim N(100,\\ \\sigma/\\sqrt n = 0.5)$. Hai biên chuẩn hoá thành $z=-3$ và $z=3$. Vậy $\\alpha = P(\\bar x < 98.5) + P(\\bar x > 101.5) = 0.00135 + (1-0.99865) = 0.0027$.</p></div>"
